  "findings": [
    "1.6.1 trains `SingleDrugElasticNet` once per drug on `scale_gene_expression` features whose `StandardScaler` is fitted on the training samples of that drug; v2 fits `scaledGeneExpression` once over all training pairs and routes by drug. The two agree (class forward) when every drug has the same training samples (`shared_enet`), and differ when the drugs were measured on different samples (`ragged_enet`). This is the intended 'globally fitted single-drug featurizers' deviation of the plan (4.4).",
    "1.6.1 builds `ElasticNet(alpha, l1_ratio)` with sklearn's solver defaults; l1_ratio 0 or 1 select Ridge or Lasso. v2 pins max_iter=2000, tol=1e-2, selection='random', random_state=0 (overridable). With sklearn's values set explicitly the per-drug coefficients agree to float32 precision.",
    "Defaults: 1.6.1 first grid point is l1_ratio=0.2, alpha=1 (grids l1_ratio 0.2/0.5/0.9, alpha 1/0.8/0.6/0.4/0.1/0.01/5); v2 defaults are l1_ratio=0.5, alpha=0.1. B5 should decide whether to match.",
    "The v2 preset uses the whole gene view (`scaledGeneExpression` without `gene_list`) while 1.6.1 selects `landmark_genes`. Compared on a pre-selected matrix; the list wiring belongs to B5.",
    "v2 features are float32; the `identical` steps feed both estimators the same float64 matrix and are exact."
  ],
